                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "crop=\"optional\"",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " without aspect → freeform crop; Skip is allowed."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "item",
                    "marker": "•",
                    "depth": 0,
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "crop=\"required\"",
                            "code": true
                        },
                        {
                            "text": " without aspect → freeform crop; Confirm is required."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Confirm stores the region the crop sheet shows: the largest rectangle at the locked aspect (or the photo's own aspect when freeform), narrowed by zoom and placed where the person moved it. The region starts centred. Drag the photo to move it and pinch or use the zoom buttons to zoom from 1× to 4×. The region never leaves the photo: it stops at the edges, and zooming out pulls it back inside. With a locked aspect that differs from the photo's, the region can move along the longer side even at 1×; freeform at 1× is the whole photo. A new pick starts centred again. Skip stores the whole photo. Image mode always stores a JPEG."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "runs": [
                        {
                            "text": "Clear, Skip, Confirm, Cancel, Crop, zoom, crop-move, and source-chooser copy are package chrome; see "
                        },
